WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
Two hectares in Kalamba stayed with Asia-United Bank after the tenants lost their claim. This

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:12.000
is unintended consequences episode 164. A court loss on a bank parcel in Laguna, the

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.040
statute written to break concentrated holdings, the zoning certificates that locked exemptions

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.380
in first, the tendency that kept the same hands on the same plots, and the funding extensions

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:28.700
that left the timing gap open. On June 30, 2021, the Philippine Supreme Court ruled in GR

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:36.960
number 226852. The parcel sat in Burangai, Mackeeling, Kalamba, Laguna. Asia United Bank owned it.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:43.080
A prior local zoning ordinance had reclassified it as industrial, and that reclassification qualified

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:49.020
the land for exemption from the Comprehensive Agrarian Reform Program. Renato Tanyan and the

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:54.320
heirs of Pio Candelaria had worked the land. They could not prove vested tenancy rights before

00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:00.340
the zoning change. They received no redistribution. The court treated a housing and land use regulatory

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:05.920
board certification of industrial zoning as conclusive. That certification removed the parcel

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:11.400
from redistribution before any tendency claim could be litigated. The exemption mechanism left

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.820
those workers on the same plots under unchanged control. The loss was not a surprise invented in 2021.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:23.700
It followed a design choice made more than 30 years earlier by people trying to stop exactly

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:29.460
this kind of concentrated rural power. After the 1986 People Power Revolution removed

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:34.740
Ferdinand Marcos, the new government under President Corazon Aquino faced intense pressure

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:38.900
to break up the concentrated rural land holdings that had fueled decades of unrest.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:47.300
Congress answered on June 10, 1988, with Republic Act number 6657, the Comprehensive Agrarian Reform

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:53.480
Law. The statute caped private ownership at five hectares per landowner. It directed the department

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:58.120
of agrarian reform to distribute excess land to tenant farmers and landless workers.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:03.460
It also required that tenants on retained or exempt parcels received leasehold protections

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:07.980
so they would no longer face arbitrary eviction or share tenancy abuses.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:13.500
Lawmakers viewed the caps in the protections as a practical way to extend the earlier presidential

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.900
decree 27 reforms while respecting constitutional property rights.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:23.100
states, sudden plantation seizures looked to them like economic disruption the country

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:23.980
could not absorb.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:29.500
The policy appeared measured and administratively feasible because it built on powers local

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:34.760
governments already had, the power to reclassify land for non-agricultural uses.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:40.020
That step seemed necessary if cities were to grow in an orderly way without dismantling

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.660
every commercial farm at once.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:47.060
Proponents reasoned that a five-hectare limit would still leave owners with viable holdings.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:52.500
On land that stayed exempt, regulated rents and written contracts would, they believed

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.360
gradually improved tenant security.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.220
The intention was security without seizure.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:02.120
The instrument was a balance between redistribution, retention, and local planning.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:07.520
The Department of Agrarian Reform began issuing certificates of Land Ownership Award in

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.460
late 1988.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:16.200
By 2012, it reported having distributed 4.49 million hectares to roughly 2.8 million beneficiaries.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:21.940
early official statements highlighted the transfer of rice and cornlands as a clear success.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:28.980
Picture that area as farmland handed on paper to millions of households who had worked other people's estates.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:38.720
The 1994 Amendments, Republic Act 78,881, carved out fish ponds, prawn farms, and certain livestock operations.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:44.160
Commercial producers had lobbied that forced redistribution would destroy export industries.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:49.760
ities. The carve-outs reflected that argument. Skeptics inside the agrarian reform bureaucracy

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:54.580
warned about a different door. Exemption clauses plus the requirement that the housing

00:03:54.580 --> 00:04:00.560
and land use regulatory board ratify local reclassifications would invite strategic rezoning

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:07.400
before coverage notices could be served. Implementation nevertheless preceded parcel-by-parcel. Municipal

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:12.200
councils could pass zoning ordinances that shifted land from agricultural to industrial

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:17.740
or residential categories. After that, the central board certification locked in the exemption,

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:23.940
even if tenants had already begun leasehold negotiations. Section 10 of the law listed explicit

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:29.700
exemptions for non-agricultural uses. Local governments treated reclassification as a routine

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:35.980
planning tool, not as an evasion tactic. The text gave them that reading. The people administering

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:41.280
the program were using the authorities the statute had placed side by side. Landowners responded

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:47.140
by securing municipal zoning ordinances that reclassified agricultural parcels as industrial,

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:52.580
residential, or commercial before the Department of Agrarian Reform could place them under coverage.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:58.420
In the Kalamba record, Asia Trust Development Bank obtained a February 2007 certification

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:03.780
from the Housing and Land Use Regulatory Board that the grassland site had already been zoned

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:10.300
industrial. The Supreme Court later treated that certification as conclusive. Similar reclassifications

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:16.180
removed hundreds of hectares in Sariaia, Kazan, even after some tenants had received certificates

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:22.480
of land ownership award. The award on paper did not stop the category change. The law also permitted

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:28.100
conversion to high-value commercial crops without triggering redistribution. Many estates simply

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:33.800
shifted from rice to bananas or pineapples and kept the same workforce under leasehold contracts.

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:39.520
Tenants remained on the identical plots, paying rent or delivering shares to the same families

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:46.140
or to corporate successors. The formal label was now exempt land. A 2009 World Bank technical

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:51.720
paper documented what those mechanisms produced together, with slow processing and credit constraints

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:58.440
on new owners. Ownership concentration remained largely intact in several provinces. The redistribution

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:04.040
had moved millions of hectares. In those provinces, the pattern of who controlled the land had not broken

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:07.200
in the way the 1988 statute was written to break it.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.220
Second order effects followed.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:14.060
Local land markets depressed because banks hesitated to land against titles that might

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:15.680
later face exemption claims.

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:17.620
Rural poverty continued.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:21.120
The poverty the original redistribution had been meant to relieve.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:24.900
A further consequence appeared among people who did receive land.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:30.120
New owners found themselves unable to consolidate fragmented holdings into efficient units.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:38.640
The same reclassification route that protected large owners also discouraged investment in irrigation or machinery on smaller redistributed plots.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:44.480
A title that might be reclassified was a hard thing to borrow against and a hard thing to improve.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:51.520
The causal chain is specific. The statute granted redistribution power and local zoning authority at the same time.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:56.960
That pairing created a timing advantage. reclassification could be finished before coverage.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:03.040
tenancy relations then survived under leasehold rules the law itself preserved on exempt parcels.

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:08.480
The relationship did not have to be illegal to outlast the reform. It only had to be renamed.

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:15.850
The 2021 decision reaffirmed the pre-program reclassification route. Future claimants must prove that

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:21.310
tenancy rights existed before any zoning change. Successive administrations have extended the

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:26.990
comprehensive agrarian reform programs funding deadlines rather than closing the exemption loopholes.

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:39.370
Some municipal governments have tightened zoning review, a research gate evaluation of 30 years of implementation notes that conversion applications continue to outpace actual redistribution in peri-urban zones.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:42.910
No large-scale reversal of earlier exemptions has occurred.

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:46.590
Legal preservation of control remains the dominant outcome.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:52.330
The same evaluation observes that poor targeting and land consolidation problems persisted

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:57.810
because the original statute never created an independent mechanism to audit whether a reclassification

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:02.010
served genuine development needs or merely shielded existing owners.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:03.710
Funding could be renewed.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.090
The timing gap did not have to be.

00:08:06.994 --> 00:08:13.034
When a statute sets a hard ownership cap and, in the same text, authorizes local reclassification

00:08:13.034 --> 00:08:14.674
ratified by a central board.

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:19.154
The actors who control the zoning calendar gain a reliable route around the cap.

00:08:19.654 --> 00:08:21.194
The cap is what the public hears.

00:08:21.194 --> 00:08:26.034
measures. The calendar is what decides which parcels ever meet it. A municipal council

00:08:26.034 --> 00:08:31.394
can move a field from agricultural to industrial on a planning agenda. A central board can

00:08:31.394 --> 00:08:36.614
then certify that change. Once the certificate exists, coverage arrives too late to matter.

00:08:37.074 --> 00:08:41.674
The measurement that counted was not acres owned on the day the law passed. It was the

00:08:41.674 --> 00:08:46.694
land use category on the day a notice could be served. When leasehold rules remain in force

00:08:46.694 --> 00:08:52.114
on every exempt parcel. The economic relationship between tenant and owner does not have to be

00:08:52.114 --> 00:08:58.094
rebuilt. It continues under a new legal heading. Rent replaces the share. A written contract

00:08:58.094 --> 00:09:03.714
replaces the old arrangement. The same family or the same corporate successor still receives

00:09:03.714 --> 00:09:08.954
the payment, and the same workers still stand on the same ground. Security of a sort is there.

00:09:09.494 --> 00:09:14.294
The transfer of control is not. Lawmakers who wrote those leasehold protections were trying

00:09:14.294 --> 00:09:18.014
to stop eviction and abuse on land, the state would not redistribute.

00:09:18.434 --> 00:09:19.894
The protections did that job.

00:09:20.434 --> 00:09:25.474
They also made the unreformed relationship lawful, durable, and easy to describe as compliance.

00:09:25.974 --> 00:09:30.914
When proof of pre-existing tenancy rights is required after the fact, the tenant who lacked

00:09:30.914 --> 00:09:34.434
formal papers at the moment of reclassification loses the claim.

00:09:35.014 --> 00:09:38.954
Work on the land is not the same thing as a vested right the court will recognize.

00:09:39.834 --> 00:09:47.594
documentation becomes the whole case, and documentation is what people without lawyers are least likely to have held on the day as zoning ordinance passed.

00:09:48.174 --> 00:09:54.474
The burden falls on the party the statute was written to reach, and it falls after the category of the land has already changed.

00:09:54.934 --> 00:10:05.874
Anyone weighing a redistribution rule now, a land cap, a housing set aside, and affordability, quote, a tide to a rezoning power, has a narrower question than whether the cap is sincere.

00:10:05.874 --> 00:10:11.194
How will any exemption or conversion procedure be timed against the moment coverage is declared?

00:10:11.614 --> 00:10:13.994
And who is positioned to finish the paperwork first?

00:10:14.454 --> 00:10:15.654
That's the case for today.

